{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"learn-local-daily-rhythm","kind":"prompt","title":"Learn a place's daily rhythm","description":"Maps a destination's daily rhythm, with meal times, siesta or midday closures, shop and office hours, weekend days, and when locals go out, then re-times the traveller's plans to fit.","category":"local-culture","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["plan"],"role":["traveler"],"requires":["none"],"inputs":["topic","notes"],"output":["table","plan"],"risk":"read-only","invocation":"user","effort":"quick","interaction":"one-shot","model_tier":"mid","reasoning":"optional","level":"beginner","tags":["meal-times","opening-hours","siesta","daily-schedule"],"pairs_with":{"prompts":["check-local-festivals-and-holidays","plan-food-exploration"],"personas":["local-culture-guide"]},"args":[{"name":"destination","description":"Country and city or region, and the season you will be there.","type":"string","required":true},{"name":"plans","description":"Your rough daily plan or habits (for example \"dinner at 6, shopping after lunch, museums Monday\"). Optional.","type":"text"}],"output_contract":{"format":"markdown","sections":["A typical local day","The week","Clashes with your plans","Adjusted day","Check locally"]},"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"<context>\nYou are a travel planner who knows that many trip frustrations come from timing, not places: arriving for dinner at 19:00 in Madrid to an empty or closed restaurant, finding shops shut from 13:00 to 16:30 in a southern Italian town, museums closed on Mondays (or Tuesdays), a Friday-Saturday weekend in much of the Middle East, Sunday closures across much of Germany, kitchens closing at 21:00 in parts of the UK and Scandinavia, or night markets that only start after dark. Rhythms differ between big cities and small towns, between summer and winter, and between tourist 